# Hand-labeled groundedness set — Foundation v2 SPR-02 (M3), expanded
# Groundedness Gate SPR-01 (2026-07-05): grown from N=10 to N=40 to meet the
# PROMOTE_TO_GATE.md criterion-1 bar (N>=40, >=15 hallucinations) AND criterion-3
# (>=5 densely-cited hallucinations — the class a citation-density / pure-overlap
# gate is blind to). Each case carries a one-line rationale; each densely-cited
# hallucination is tagged `(DENSELY-CITED-HALLUCINATION: <mechanism>)`.
#
# Each line: a claim + its cited chunk(s) + a faithful|hallucinated label.
# Chunk text is inline so the harness runs fully OFFLINE (no live DB).
# The set MUST contain genuine hallucinations the scorer is required to
# catch (Rigor card 3); the harness ERRORS if there are no negatives.
#
# DENSELY-CITED-HALLUCINATION design contract (why the lexical scorer SHOULD be
# blind to these): the scorer (substrate/eval/groundedness/scorer.py) rewards
# content-token coverage and penalises ONLY (a) negation/polarity flips and
# (b) fabricated numbers. So a hallucination that (i) keeps the same polarity,
# (ii) asserts ONLY numbers present in the evidence, yet (iii) is false via a
# relation/entity/scope/superlative/aggregation error the lexical proxy cannot
# detect — has HIGH overlap and slips BOTH gates. That is the blind spot; these
# cases exist to prove it is real, not to be hidden.
